I was playing a Samurai, trying to extend ascension streak to five.
Had some early game hiccups like getting lycanthropy and destroying my
GDSM, and also stupidly thinking my starting katana was just the
Japanese name for  "long sword" and drying up most of the fountains
wondering why it wasn't turning into Excalibur. (On the upside, I
turned one of my #monster-summoned pet wolves into a black dragon, and
unexpectedly got a wish from one of the upper-level fountains.)

Anyway, I straightened all that out, was dual-weaponing Grayswandir
with a katana and taking most everything out in one or two hits. Tons
of healing potions dropped by monsters who never had a chance to quaff
them, so I alchemized up to 450HP, and still had a good dozen full
healing left over. Though I'd told myself that I should stop trying to
make every character into a spellcaster, I traded my cloak of
displacement for a robe in the Sanctum and using a luxury wish on a
Helm of Brilliance, so I could use magic missile (stupid - I'd already
taken out all the krakens in Wiz Tower) and jumping at 0% on Astral.
Unfortunately, I hadn't found a book of cure sickenss, but I had so
many full healing potions, surely I wouldn't need it, right? Right?

Got to Astral without much incident. First two altars were wrong (I
refuse to exploit the astral call bug). Last one was guarded by
Pestilence, and Dave the Tourist wielding... Vorpal Blade. Teleported
Dave away as much as possible, eventually tried to shoot him with a
wand of death but he, of course, had a shield of reflection. Meanwhile
I'm inching my way toward that lawful altar, with Pestilence hot on my
tail. He catches up and starts inflicting disease. I start quaffing. I
run out of potions. I start using the unihorn. I pray once. Something
has stunned me, an Angel is on the other side, I have nowhere to
escape.

I save with 32HP left and ponder my possibilities. They aren't good. I
have two amulets of life saving, but am wearing an amulet of
reflection, and won't have time to switch. I have a few more full
healing potions in my bag - why weren't they all in main inventory??
Surely the likelihood of stepping on a fire trap or getting hit by
Frost Brand or some such was not worth keeping so many potions sacked
up. I sigh, start the game up again, get the potions out, and, as
expected, die before I have a chance to quaff.

OK, full healing in bag was one of only many mistakes; others
included:

- Should have swapped ring of slow digestion for ring of free action;
would have reduced stunning and allowed me to take out Pestilence
efficiently and (hopefully) with time left to cure disease. (Was
wearing ring of conflict on other hand, pet guardian Angel having long
since expired.)

- Should have used my copious wands of teleportation more liberally to
get other monsters out of the way.

- Should have tried harder not to be Burdened. I know, people always
say being Burdened on Astral is suicide, but I've ascended 11 times
this year and was only unburdened once or twice. However, I also
managed to avoid Pestilence almost completely in those other games.
Here, more speed could definitely have saved my life.

- Should have waited to pray until all potions in inventory were
consumed. Would have still been stunned, likely, but would have
restored full hit points and removed illness.

Damn, I was literally steps from the altar. I almost wish Dave had
killed me with Vorpy; would have been a more interesting death than
"Killed by an Angel of Moloch" (though Pesty really gets the credit).
At least I finished with +8 (!) Fire Brand, grabbed from the corpse of
another player-monster, which was kind of a cool consolation prize...

